# WordPress PHP Conventions

See `edminboost-compliance.mdc` for the security gate; `edminboost-command-center.mdc` for CC patterns.

## File Header

Every PHP file must start with:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Brief description.
 *
 * @package EdminBoost
 */

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}
```

## Security

- Check capabilities before rendering admin pages: `current_user_can( EDMINBOOST_Settings::CAPABILITY )`.
- Escape output: `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_html_e()`.
- Sanitize all settings via `EDMINBOOST_Settings::sanitize()` as `sanitize_callback` in `register_setting()`.
- Settings API: `show_in_rest => false`, `wp_unslash()` on array input in sanitize.
- Use nonces for custom form/AJAX handlers (`wp_nonce_field`, `check_admin_referer`).

## I18N

- User-facing strings: `__()`, `_e()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_attr__()`, etc. with `EDMINBOOST_TEXT_DOMAIN` (equals `EDMINBOOST_PLUGIN_SLUG` / header `Text Domain`: `edminboost-admin-customization`).
- Do not use the short `edminboost` hook prefix as the text domain — Plugin Check expects the header domain to match the plugin slug.
- Do not use legacy domains (e.g. `edminboost-smart-admin-productivity-tool`) — only `edminboost-admin-customization` matches `EDMINBOOST_TEXT_DOMAIN` and the plugin header.
- Do not call `load_plugin_textdomain()` from plugin code — header `Text Domain` + `Domain Path: /languages` is enough (WordPress 4.6+; required for Plugin Check). `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()` does not register a textdomain loader.
- `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Base::get_name()` / `get_description()` use the literal slug `'edminboost-admin-customization'` in each `__()` call (not the constant).

## WordPress APIs

- Register hooks in `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()` or feature `register_hooks()` — not in the bootstrap file.
- Privileged AJAX: `wp_ajax_edminboost_cc_drawer_preview` on premium `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Bar_Pro` (Layout Studio drawer preview); `wp_ajax_edminboost_save_settings` on `EDMINBOOST_Admin` (CC + settings AJAX save); `wp_ajax_edminboost_load_cc_page` on `EDMINBOOST_Admin` (CC tab HTML without full reload); `wp_ajax_edminboost_export_settings` / `wp_ajax_edminboost_import_settings` on `EDMINBOOST_Admin_Licensed` when `has_licensed_admin_ui()` (delegates to `EDMINBOOST_Admin`).
- Use Settings API for options (`register_setting`, `add_settings_section`, `add_settings_field`).
- Enqueue assets with `EDMINBOOST_VERSION` as the version string.
- Pass data to JS via `wp_localize_script()` — `edminboostData` on plugin screens (includes `themeSettings`, `presets`, `themePresets`, `roleMatrix`, `ccNav`, `settingsSave`, etc.); `edminboostCcBar` on the live CC bar drawer script. AJAX save (`ajax_save_settings`) returns `theme`, `active_layout_preset`, refreshed `presets`, and related keys via `build_ajax_save_response()`.
- Page slugs: use `EDMINBOOST_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` and `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center::PAGE_*` suffixes.

## Class Wiring

- Bootstrap requires core classes (including `EDMINBOOST_Plan`); instantiate only via `edminboost_run_plugin()`. Dev tree bootstrap omits `includes/pro/`; premium release zip injects `edminboost-premium.php` at build time (`bin/build-zip-lib.sh`). When `EDMINBOOST_Plan::is_direct_build()`, readable `edminboost-pro-package.php` loads pro modules before `EDMINBOOST_Plugin` is constructed. PHPUnit loads `edminboost-premium.php` when `includes/pro/` exists unless `EDMINBOOST_TEST_WPORG=1` (see `tests/bootstrap.php`).
- `EDMINBOOST_Plugin` constructor: `EDMINBOOST_Features`, `EDMINBOOST_Admin`.
- Command Center: `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center` (static helpers + `register_hooks()`).
- Command Center Bar: `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Bar::register_hooks()` in `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()` — redirect-only on free/WP.org; drawer/badge paths delegate to `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Bar_Pro` when licensed. Role visibility on the live bar: filter `edminboost_top_bar_items_for_user` in `get_items_for_current_user()` (premium: `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Role_Visibility_Pro`).
- Command Center role visibility (premium): `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Role_Visibility_Pro::register_hooks()` from `edminboost-pro-package.php` — not loaded on WordPress.org zips.
- Licensed settings sanitize (premium): `EDMINBOOST_Settings_Sanitize_Pro::register_hooks()` — `edminboost_sanitize_command_center`, `edminboost_sanitize_features`, `edminboost_sanitize_custom_presets` when `has_licensed_admin_ui()`.
- Licensed setting help (premium): `EDMINBOOST_Setting_Help_Pro::register_hooks()` — `edminboost_setting_help_tooltips`.
- Menu Studio: `EDMINBOOST_Menu_Studio::register_hooks()` in `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()`.
- Visual theme: `EDMINBOOST_Theme::register_hooks()` in `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()`; scheduled dark mode runtime via `EDMINBOOST_Theme_Pro` when licensed.
- White label: `EDMINBOOST_White_Label` in premium package — hooks via `EDMINBOOST_Plan_Gating::register_pro_runtime_modules()` when licensed.
- Plan / Pro: use `EDMINBOOST_Plan::is_direct_build()`, `has_licensed_admin_ui()`, `include_preset_in_ui()`, `render_admin_extension( $slot )` in shared partials (`render_admin_extension()` is a no-op when unlicensed). Premium-only logic lives in `includes/pro/` (`EDMINBOOST_Pro`, `EDMINBOOST_Admin_Licensed`, `EDMINBOOST_Plan_Licensing`, `EDMINBOOST_Plan_Limits`, `EDMINBOOST_Plan_Gating`). Omit licensed partial slots on free/unlicensed builds (no locked upsell UI). Licensed-only partials that are not extension slots: include via `is_readable()` under `admin/partials/pro/` (e.g. overview top bar link meta, theme licensed description, animation speed field). See `edminboost-compliance.mdc`.
- Licensed admin menus: action `edminboost_register_admin_menus` — `EDMINBOOST_Admin_Licensed::register_submenus()` registers Settings and White Label when `has_licensed_admin_ui()`; page HTML/titles via `edminboost_render_cc_page` / `edminboost_cc_page_title` (also used by CC tab AJAX in `capture_cc_page_html()`).
- Setting help: `EDMINBOOST_Setting_Help` — static helpers only; required in bootstrap; `get_tooltips()` applies `edminboost_setting_help_tooltips` (premium: `EDMINBOOST_Setting_Help_Pro`); `should_show()` includes Dashboard setup wizard until `is_setup_complete()`.
- Admin submenu order: `EDMINBOOST_Admin::normalize_plugin_submenu()` on `admin_menu` priority 999 in `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()`.
- Plugins screen row meta: `plugin_row_meta` → `EDMINBOOST_Admin::add_plugin_row_meta()` adds Docs link (`EDMINBOOST_PLUGIN_DOCS_URL`, `target="_blank"`, `rel="noopener noreferrer"`).
- Admin page titles: `EDMINBOOST_Admin::register_plugin_submenu_page()` / `bind_admin_page_title()` set `$title` on `load-{hook}` (fixes PHP 8.1+ warnings for tab-only pages with null parent).
- New productivity modules: extend `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Base`, register in `EDMINBOOST_Features`; defaults/enable/sanitize via `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Settings` (see `edminboost-features.mdc`).
- Settings: `EDMINBOOST_Settings::get()`, `::get_form_defaults()` (normalized plugin defaults for admin form reset — no `edminboost_settings` filter), `::strip_free_build_product_features()` (WP.org read/sanitize guard — Pro-only keys including `role_visibility` stripped when `! EDMINBOOST_Plan::is_direct_build()`), `::is_enabled()`, `::is_feature_enabled()`, `::get_feature_settings()`; feature shape helpers in `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Settings`. `sanitize_command_center()` applies `edminboost_sanitize_command_center` (premium: `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Role_Visibility_Pro` + `EDMINBOOST_Settings_Sanitize_Pro` when licensed). Pro-shaped top bar, behavior, theme schedule, and menu fields sanitize in premium package only — core CC sanitize stays WP.org-safe. `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Settings::sanitize()` ends with `edminboost_sanitize_features` (premium: login redirects when licensed).
- Activation seeds defaults via `EDMINBOOST_Activator`; deactivation is a no-op.

